menu "Round recorder"

    config REC_SECONDS
        int "Seconds kept, and saved with each Save"
        range 10 300
        default 180
        help
            How much audio the board holds, and so how long each saved clip
            is. Each second takes 8 KB of flash and 16 KB of PSRAM (the ring
            and a save's copy of it). 180 s gives 14 slots in the 32 MB
            flash, 60 s gives 41. Changing it changes the size of the slots
            in flash, so clips saved before may be lost.

    config REC_KEEP_MAX_S
        int "Longest recording, seconds"
        range 60 3000
        default 900
        help
            Save keeps what's held and goes on recording until Save comes
            again, or until the recording is this long. It's written in
            parts the length of what's held, one slot each, and always
            leaves at least one slot to the other recordings.

    config REC_LOW_BATTERY_PCT
        int "On battery, save and power off at this charge (percent)"
        range 0 20
        default 3
        help
            Below it, off USB, the board saves what it's holding (or ends
            the recording going on) and powers off, so the battery running
            out doesn't lose it. 0 turns this off.

    config REC_SOUNDS
        bool "Sounds when a recording starts, stops or fails"
        default y
        help
            Two short notes on the speaker: up for a start, down for a
            stop, low for a save that failed. Heard in a pocket, and left
            in the recording as a marker. Until it's changed in Settings.

    config REC_MIC_GAIN_DB
        int "Microphone gain (dB)"
        range 0 36
        default 30
        help
            The ES7210's gain, in 3 dB steps, until it's changed in
            Settings on the board. Lower it if loud voices clip.

    config REC_VOLUME
        int "Speaker volume for playback (0-100)"
        range 0 100
        default 70
        help
            Until it's changed in Settings on the board.

    config REC_SCREEN_OFF_S
        int "Screen off after this many seconds without a touch"
        range 5 600
        default 15
        help
            Until it's changed in Settings on the board.

endmenu
